What is warp knitted lining? Warp-knitted lining is a kind of adhesive lining, and some people call it double-sided elastic; The warp spread is processed as the basic coating, and the warp spread is relatively simple. Generally, the warp yarns are crocheted with each other and inserted in the weft direction, which makes the warp spread soft and elastic.
Characteristics and uses of warp knitted lining;
1. The processing technology is simple, and the weave of the base cloth is mostly used as the warp knitting cloth for processing the lining cloth. The weave structure is simple, and the weave is mostly knitted by warp yarns in the weft direction, so the Chen Ben is low and the efficiency is high;
2. It is safe and environment-friendly. The warp-knitted liner does not need resin finishing and does not contain formaldehyde. Because of its short technological process and less pollution during processing, the warp-knitted liner can be called an environment-friendly lining cloth.
3. The base fabric of warp knitted liner is made of polyester filament or viscose yarn, which is flat in warp direction, good in drapability, good in weft direction, soft in hand feeling, strong in randomness and suitable for elastic fabrics.
4. that excellent characteristic of warp knitted fabric make the style variety of adhesive lining processed by warp knitted fabric varied, which can meet the requirement of fabrics with different textures and styles from light to heavy, fully meet the various requirements of various fabrics and garments for adhesive lining, and has wide application.
